        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor: centralize bounded file reads in fs-safe",
        "body": "Related: #110594\nRelated: #110591\nRelated: #110592\nRelated: #110516\nRelated: openclaw/fs-safe#41\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw owned duplicate asynchronous and synchronous loops for allocation-bounded reads from file descriptors that had already been opened and pinned by a filesystem boundary. That duplicated policy now owned by fs-safe and made the byte-limit/error contract easier for the two implementations to drift.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis routes all seven descriptor-read consumers through the existing boundary-file facade and delegates incremental reads to the published fs-safe advanced API. The facade preserves OpenClaw's shipped `RangeError` message for oversized files, while the duplicate 63-line reader is deleted.\n\nThe dependency is pinned to `@openclaw/fs-safe@0.4.2`. OpenClaw's downstream `EPERM` fsync patch and patch allowlist entry are removed because that compatibility fix now ships upstream. Both lockfiles and the Plugin SDK API baseline are regenerated from the published artifact.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no intended user-visible behavior change. Config input, secrets plans, agent message files, local avatars, hook metadata, and workspace bootstrap files retain their existing size limits and overflow messages while sharing fs-safe's allocation-bounded implementation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Published dependency: [@openclaw/fs-safe@0.4.2](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@openclaw/fs-safe/v/0.4.2), [GitHub Release](https://github.com/openclaw/fs-safe/releases/tag/v0.4.2), integrity `sha512-x02inO/FF+kuKU8W5vX5UFgkkMG2bCf2u02lX90XQYCYzvD87P/J0F9dfYKF4o/9b37JATdXcUhJwrhtREpwWQ==`.\n- fs-safe exact release CI: [Node 22/24 matrix](https://github.com/openclaw/fs-safe/actions/runs/29670278662) and [coverage](https://github.com/openclaw/fs-safe/actions/runs/29670278645); isolated Node 24 proof passed all 433 runnable tests with 5 platform skips.\n- OpenClaw focused Testbox proof passed formatting, the package-patch guard, Plugin SDK API baseline validation, targeted Oxlint, and both async/sync boundary-reader regression tests.\n- Full `pnpm check:changed` passed at head `cb345481401d6bf55e40974245279d1f93345259`, including all shrinkwrap guards, Plugin SDK contracts, the complete TypeScript project graph, all Oxlint shards, and runtime import-cycle validation.\n- Fresh whole-branch Codex autoreview reported no accepted/actionable findings (correctness confidence 0.90). A focused review of the final lint fix was clean at 0.98.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the implementation, dependency source/API, generated artifacts, and test evidence.\n",
